8. ENERGY CALCULATIONS
======================

Implement energy calculations correctly.

Active power:

P(kW) = Voltage(V) × Current(A) × Power Factor / 1000

Energy:

Energy(kWh) = Power(kW) × Time(hours)

For interval-based telemetry:

Energy(kWh) = Power(kW) × Interval(seconds) / 3600

Electricity cost:

Cost(INR) = Energy(kWh) × Tariff(INR/kWh)

Calculate:

* Machine-level energy consumption
* Factory-level energy consumption
* Daily consumption
* Weekly consumption
* Monthly consumption
* Estimated electricity cost
* Peak demand
* Average power demand
* Idle energy consumption
* Energy consumption by machine category

Avoid double-counting cumulative energy.

Prefer validated meter energy readings when available.

Clearly document assumptions.

For three-phase systems, implement the appropriate measurement formula only when the sensor data and wiring configuration support it.

Do not treat a single-phase approximation as a validated three-phase measurement.

